 : <a href=\"./Init/Data/Float/Float32.html#Float32\">Float32</a>)</span></span> <span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">C</span> : <span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"./BLAS/Float32/Mat.html#BLAS.Float32.Mat\">Mat</a> <span class=\"fn\">m</span> <span class=\"fn\">n</span></span>)</span></span> <span class=\"decl_args\"> :</span><div class=\"decl_type\"><span class=\"fn\"><span class=\"fn\">(<a href=\"./BLAS/Float32/Gemm.html#BLAS.Float32.Mat.gemm\">gemm</a> <span class=\"fn\">α</span> <span class=\"fn\">A</span> <span class=\"fn\">B</span> <span class=\"fn\">β</span> <span class=\"fn\">C</span>)</span>.<a href=\"./BLAS/Float32/Mat.html#BLAS.Float32.Mat.data\">data</a></span> <a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Eq\">=</a> <span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"./BLAS/Float32/Mat.html#BLAS.Float32.mapMat\">mapMat</a> <span class=\"fn\"><span class=\"fn\">C</span>.<a href=\"./BLAS/Float32/Mat.html#BLAS.Float32.Mat.data\">data</a></span> <span class=\"fn\"><span class=\"fn\">C</span>.<a href=\"./BLAS/Float32/Mat.html#BLAS.Float32.Mat.off\">off</a></span> <span class=\"fn\"><span class=\"fn\">C</span>.<a href=\"./BLAS/Float32/Mat.html#BLAS.Float32.Mat.ld\">ld</a></span> <span class=\"fn\">m</span> <span class=\"fn\">0</span> <span class=\"fn\">n</span> <span class=\"fn\">(<a href=\"./BLAS/Float32/Gemm.html#BLAS.Float32.Mat.gemmAt\">gemmAt</a> <span class=\"fn\">α</span> <span class=\"fn\">A</span> <span class=\"fn\">B</span> <span class=\"fn\">β</span> <span class=\"fn\">C</span>)</span></span></div></div>","info":{"doc":"The array of `gemm α A B β C` is the array of `C` with its elements updated.","docLink":"./BLAS/Float32/Gemm.html#BLAS.Float32.Mat.data_gemm","kind":"theorem","line":229,"name":"BLAS.Float32.Mat.data_gemm","sourceLink":"https://github.com/fgdorais/lean4-blas/blob/0b5b806802a404d62a8c76bf36594f35690cd2ba/BLAS/Float32/Gemm.lean#L229-L234"}},{"header":"<div class=\"decl_header\"><span class=\"decl_kind\">def</span><span class=\"decl_name\"> <a class=\"break_within\" href=\"./BLAS/Float32/Gemm.html#BLAS.Float32.Mat.gemm\"><span class=\"name\">BLAS</span>.<span class=\"name\">Float32</span>.<span class=\"name\">Mat</span>.<span class=\"name\">gemm</span></a> </span><span class=\"impl_arg\"><span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">{<span class=\"fn\">m </span><span class=\"fn\">n </span><span class=\"fn\">k</span> : <a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Nat\">Nat</a>}</span></span> </span><span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">α</span> : <a href=\"./Init/Data/Float/Float32.html#Float32\">Float32</a>)</span></span> <span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">A</span> : <span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"./BLAS/Float32/Mat.html#BLAS.Float32.Mat\">Mat</a> <span class=\"fn\">m</span> <span class=\"fn\">k</span></span>)</span></span> <span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">B</span> : <span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"./BLAS/Float32/Mat.html#BLAS.Float32.Mat\">Mat</a> <span class=\"fn\">k</span> <span class=\"fn\">n</span></span>)</span></span> <span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">β</span> : <a href=\"./Init/Data/Float/Float32.html#Float32\">Float32</a>)</span></span> <span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">C</span> : <span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"./BLAS/Float32/Mat.html#BLAS.Float32.Mat\">Mat</a> <span class=\"fn\">m</span> <span class=\"fn\">n</span></span>)</span></span> <span class=\"decl_args\"> :</span><div class=\"decl_type\"><span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"./BLAS/Float32/Mat.html#BLAS.Float32.Mat\">Mat</a> <span class=\"fn\">m</span> <span class=\"fn\">n</span></span></div></div>","info":{"doc":"`gemm α A B β C` is `α * A * B + β * C`, over `C`, by the blocked loops of `PMat.gemmBlocked`. Each\nelement gets the operations of the naive loops of the reference BLAS, in the same order, so the\nresult is that of `gemmNaive` to the bit, about twice as fast. It updates `C` in place when `C` is\npacked and its array is not shared. It leaves the elements of `C`'s array outside `C` unchanged. As\nin the reference BLAS, it sets `C` to `0` without reading it when `β = 0`, before adding the\nproducts, and only scales `C` when `α = 0`, without reading `A` or `B`.","docLink":"./BLAS/Float32/Gemm.html#BLAS.Float32.Mat.gemm","kind":"def","line":203,"name":"BLAS.Float32.Mat.gemm","sourceLink":"https://github.com/fgdorais/lean4-blas/blob/0b5b806802a404d62a8c76bf36594f35690cd2ba/BLAS/Float32/Gemm.lean#L203-L227"}},{"header":"<div class=\"decl_header\"><span class=\"decl_kind\">theorem</span><span class=\"decl_name\"> <a class=\"break_within\" href=\"./BLAS/Float32/Gemm.html#BLAS.Float32.Mat.getElem_gemmNaive\"><span class=\"name\">BLAS</span>.<span class=\"name\">Float32</span>.<span class=\"name\">Mat</span>.<span class=\"name\">getElem_gemmNaive</span></a> </span><span class=\"impl_arg\"><span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">{<span class=\"fn\">m </span><span class=\"fn\">n </span><span class=\"fn\">k</span> : <a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Nat\">Nat</a>}</span></span> </span><span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">α</span> : <a href=\"./Init/Data/Float/Float32.html#Float32\">Float32</a>)</span></span> <span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">A</span> : <span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"./BLAS/Float32/Mat.html#BLAS.Float32.Mat\">Mat</a> <span class=\"fn\">m</span> <span class=\"fn\">k</span></span>)</span></span> <span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">B</span> : <span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"./BLAS/Float32/Mat.html#BLAS.Float32.Mat\">Mat</a> <span class=\"fn\">k</span> <span class=\"fn\">n</span></span>)</span></span> <span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">β</span> : <a href=\"./Init/Data/Float/Float32.html#Float32\">Float32</a>)</span></span> <span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">C</span> : <span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"./BLAS/Float32/Mat.html#BLAS.Float32.Mat\">