ss=\"decl_kind\">def</span><span class=\"decl_name\"> <a class=\"break_within\" href=\"./BLAS/Float32/Gemm.html#BLAS.Float32.Mat.gemmNaive\"><span class=\"name\">BLAS</span>.<span class=\"name\">Float32</span>.<span class=\"name\">Mat</span>.<span class=\"name\">gemmNaive</span></a> </span><span class=\"impl_arg\"><span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">{<span class=\"fn\">m </span><span class=\"fn\">n </span><span class=\"fn\">k</span> : <a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Nat\">Nat</a>}</span></span> </span><span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">α</span> : <a href=\"./Init/Data/Float/Float32.html#Float32\">Float32</a>)</span></span> <span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">A</span> : <span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"./BLAS/Float32/Mat.html#BLAS.Float32.Mat\">Mat</a> <span class=\"fn\">m</span> <span class=\"fn\">k</span></span>)</span></span> <span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">B</span> : <span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"./BLAS/Float32/Mat.html#BLAS.Float32.Mat\">Mat</a> <span class=\"fn\">k</span> <span class=\"fn\">n</span></span>)</span></span> <span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">β</span> : <a href=\"./Init/Data/Float/Float32.html#Float32\">Float32</a>)</span></span> <span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">C</span> : <span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"./BLAS/Float32/Mat.html#BLAS.Float32.Mat\">Mat</a> <span class=\"fn\">m</span> <span class=\"fn\">n</span></span>)</span></span> <span class=\"decl_args\"> :</span><div class=\"decl_type\"><span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"./BLAS/Float32/Mat.html#BLAS.Float32.Mat\">Mat</a> <span class=\"fn\">m</span> <span class=\"fn\">n</span></span></div></div>","info":{"doc":"`gemmNaive α A B β C` is `α * A * B + β * C`, by the naive loops of the reference BLAS, over `C`,\nand `gemm` computes the same matrix faster. It\nupdates `C` in place when `C` is packed and its array is not shared. It leaves the elements of\n`C`'s array outside `C` unchanged. As in the reference BLAS, it sets `C` to `0` without reading it\nwhen `β = 0`, before adding the products, and only scales `C` when `α = 0`, without reading `A` or\n`B`.","docLink":"./BLAS/Float32/Gemm.html#BLAS.Float32.Mat.gemmNaive","kind":"def","line":141,"name":"BLAS.Float32.Mat.gemmNaive","sourceLink":"https://github.com/fgdorais/lean4-blas/blob/0b5b806802a404d62a8c76bf36594f35690cd2ba/BLAS/Float32/Gemm.lean#L141-L164"}},{"header":"<div class=\"decl_header\"><span class=\"decl_kind\">theorem</span><span class=\"decl_name\"> <a class=\"break_within\" href=\"./BLAS/Float32/Gemm.html#BLAS.Float32.Mat.gemmBy_eq\"><span class=\"name\">BLAS</span>.<span class=\"name\">Float32</span>.<span class=\"name\">Mat</span>.<span class=\"name\">gemmBy_eq</span></a> </span><span class=\"impl_arg\"><span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">{<span class=\"fn\">m </span><span class=\"fn\">n </span><span class=\"fn\">k</span> : <a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Nat\">Nat</a>}</span></span> </span><span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">α </span><span class=\"fn\">β</span> : <a href=\"./Init/Data/Float/Float32.html#Float32\">Float32</a>)</span></span> <span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">f</span> : <span class=\"fn\"><span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"./BLAS/Float32/PMat.html#BLAS.Float32.PMat\">PMat</a> <span class=\"fn\">m</span> <span class=\"fn\">k</span></span> → <span class=\"fn\"><span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"./BLAS/Float32/PMat.html#BLAS.Float32.PMat\">PMat</a> <span class=\"fn\">k</span> <span class=\"fn\">n</span></span> → <span class=\"fn\"><span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"./BLAS/Float32/PMat.html#BLAS.Float32.PMat\">PMat</a> <span class=\"fn\">m</span> <span class=\"fn\">n</span></span> → <span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"./BLAS/Float32/PMat.html#BLAS.Float32.PMat\">PMat</a> <span class=\"fn\">m</span> <span class=\"fn\">n</span></span></span></span></span>)</span></span> <span class=\"decl_args\"><span